1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,090
Beijing, April 19, 2026,

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:06,200
7:30 in the morning.

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:11,240
A 1.69-metre humanoid robot
sets off on a half marathon.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,163
It crosses the line in 50 minutes

5
00:00:14,163 --> 00:00:15,560
and 26 seconds.

6
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:17,584
The human world record,

7
00:00:17,584 --> 00:00:19,857
set a month earlier in Lisbon,

8
00:00:19,857 --> 00:00:22,760
is 57 minutes and 20 seconds.

9
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:23,949
A year earlier,

10
00:00:23,949 --> 00:00:25,286
in the same race,

11
00:00:25,286 --> 00:00:27,960
the winner had taken 2 hours 40.

12
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,094
This robot doesn't come out of

13
00:00:30,094 --> 00:00:32,445
Silicon Valley. It was designed by

14
00:00:32,445 --> 00:00:35,400
Honor, a Chinese smartphone maker.

15
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:37,103
For 40 years,

16
00:00:37,103 --> 00:00:39,240
we kept saying that China copied.

17
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:43,560
Today, it's the country we
watch to guess what comes next.

18
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:46,340
To understand how we got

19
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,140
here, we have to go back to a country

20
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:51,320
where people lived on less
than half a dollar a day.

21
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,700
1978.

22
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:58,790
According to the World Bank,

23
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:01,241
income per person in China is

24
00:01:01,241 --> 00:01:03,420
157 dollars a year.

25
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:07,247
That year, Deng Xiaoping
launches the policy

26
00:01:07,247 --> 00:01:09,180
of reform and opening up.

27
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,291
The Party keeps power,

28
00:01:11,291 --> 00:01:13,680
but it lets the market in through

29
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,940
small doors.

30
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:18,304
The first one opens in 1980,

31
00:01:18,304 --> 00:01:20,456
right across from Hong Kong:

32
00:01:20,456 --> 00:01:23,500
the Shenzhen Special Economic Zone.

33
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:28,504
In 1979, about 300,000 people live

34
00:01:28,504 --> 00:01:29,740
in this area.

35
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:34,060
By the end of 2025, there
are over 18 million.

36
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:37,014
Shenzhen makes things for others first,

37
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:38,300
then for itself.

38
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:42,620
Huawei, Tencent and BYD were born there.

39
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:43,964
In 40 years,

40
00:01:43,964 --> 00:01:46,734
nearly 800 million Chinese people

41
00:01:46,734 --> 00:01:48,540
have escaped extreme poverty.

42
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:51,044
That's almost three quarters of the fall

43
00:01:51,044 --> 00:01:53,500
in poverty worldwide over that period.

44
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,405
And in 2025,

45
00:01:55,405 --> 00:01:59,500
income per person tops 13,800 dollars.

46
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:04,300
Nearly 90 times the 1978 figure.

47
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,023
For a long time, the West
reassured itself with

48
00:02:10,023 --> 00:02:11,828
a simple idea: China manufactures,

49
00:02:11,828 --> 00:02:13,440
but it doesn't invent.

50
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,320
January 2025.

51
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,990
A young company from Hangzhou,

52
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:23,760
DeepSeek, releases an AI model called R1.

53
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,120
It holds its own against
the best American models.

54
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,928
DeepSeek says it spent about 5.6 million

55
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:33,153
dollars of computing on its base

56
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:36,160
model, a figure some analysts dispute.

57
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,214
All of it on chips restricted

58
00:02:38,214 --> 00:02:40,000
by American export controls.

59
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:42,128
On Monday, January 27,

60
00:02:42,128 --> 00:02:46,480
Nvidia loses about 589 billion
dollars in market value.

61
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,798
No company had ever lost that much in

62
00:02:49,798 --> 00:02:50,960
a single day.

63
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:54,000
This shock didn't come out of nowhere.

64
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:59,275
Australia's ASPI institute
tracks 74 critical technologies.

65
00:02:59,595 --> 00:03:02,142
In the most-cited research
published between

66
00:03:02,142 --> 00:03:04,393
2021 and 2025,

67
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:07,355
China leads in 69 of them.

68
00:03:07,675 --> 00:03:09,755
In the mid-2000s,

69
00:03:09,755 --> 00:03:11,195
it led in just 3.

70
00:03:13,695 --> 00:03:15,629
But AI without electricity

71
00:03:15,629 --> 00:03:18,015
is just a program waiting to run.

72
00:03:18,335 --> 00:03:20,132
And on electricity,

73
00:03:20,132 --> 00:03:22,255
the gap is dizzying.

74
00:03:22,575 --> 00:03:25,757
In 2025, China connected more than

75
00:03:25,757 --> 00:03:29,215
430 gigawatts of wind and solar.

76
00:03:29,535 --> 00:03:31,135
In a single year.

77
00:03:31,455 --> 00:03:32,839
For the first time,

78
00:03:32,839 --> 00:03:34,946
wind and solar overtake

79
00:03:34,946 --> 00:03:37,775
thermal power plants in its power mix.

80
00:03:38,095 --> 00:03:41,186
Its renewable output reaches about 4,000

81
00:03:41,186 --> 00:03:42,655
billion kilowatt-hours.

82
00:03:42,975 --> 00:03:45,929
More than all the electricity used by

83
00:03:45,929 --> 00:03:48,255
the 27 countries of the European Union.

84
00:03:48,575 --> 00:03:52,015
That electricity then has to be stored.

85
00:03:52,335 --> 00:03:54,820
According to the
International Energy Agency,

86
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:56,796
more than 80% of the battery

87
00:03:56,796 --> 00:03:59,846
cells produced worldwide in 2025

88
00:03:59,846 --> 00:04:00,975
came from China.

89
00:04:01,295 --> 00:04:03,399
And for the materials inside

90
00:04:03,399 --> 00:04:05,935
those batteries, its share is even higher.

91
00:04:08,435 --> 00:04:10,395
From batteries to cars,

92
00:04:10,395 --> 00:04:11,795
it's only a short step.

93
00:04:12,115 --> 00:04:15,679
In 2025, nearly 3 out of 4 electric cars

94
00:04:15,679 --> 00:04:18,141
produced in the world

95
00:04:18,141 --> 00:04:19,955
came out of Chinese factories.

96
00:04:20,275 --> 00:04:21,370
That same year,

97
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:24,143
BYD, a company founded in Shenzhen in

98
00:04:24,143 --> 00:04:27,573
1995 to make batteries,

99
00:04:27,573 --> 00:04:32,755
sold 2.26 million fully electric cars.

100
00:04:33,075 --> 00:04:36,515
Tesla delivered 1.64 million.

101
00:04:36,835 --> 00:04:39,427
For the first time over a full

102
00:04:39,427 --> 00:04:41,875
year, the American company was overtaken.

103
00:04:42,195 --> 00:04:43,342
In the factories,

104
00:04:43,342 --> 00:04:45,635
machines are taking over too.

105
00:04:45,955 --> 00:04:49,232
In 2024, China installed 295,000

106
00:04:49,232 --> 00:04:51,235
industrial robots.

107
00:04:51,555 --> 00:04:55,315
More than one in every two
installed on the planet.

108
00:04:55,635 --> 00:04:57,329
And for the first time,

109
00:04:57,329 --> 00:05:00,195
most of them came from Chinese makers.

110
00:05:00,515 --> 00:05:03,302
The half-marathon humanoids are only

111
00:05:03,302 --> 00:05:05,075
the shop window of this shift.

112
00:05:07,575 --> 00:05:10,573
American investor Ray Dalio studied five

113
00:05:10,573 --> 00:05:11,796
centuries of empires:

114
00:05:11,796 --> 00:05:14,610
the Dutch Republic, then Britain,

115
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:15,895
then the United States.

116
00:05:16,215 --> 00:05:20,855
For him, power follows a big cycle.

117
00:05:21,175 --> 00:05:23,217
You rise by educating,

118
00:05:23,217 --> 00:05:25,815
